# WoW addon AI — performance

When writing or editing addon code, follow `06-notes/addon-dev/performance-and-resources.md`.

## Must

- Prefer `RegisterEvent` / `RegisterUnitEvent` and `C_Timer` over `OnUpdate`
- Any `OnUpdate` must be throttled and cleared when the UI is hidden or the feature is off
- Create frames once (or via a pool); never `CreateFrame` inside frequent refresh loops
- Use `local` aliases for APIs in hot paths; `wipe` and reuse tables
- Cancel timers / use generation counters so stale callbacks do nothing
- Bound SavedVariables growth; do not persist rebuildable caches by default
- Respect addon-message size and rate limits — no per-frame heartbeats

## Must not

- Register the broadest events and filter everything in Lua when `RegisterUnitEvent` exists
- Leave debug `print` / dump loops on hot paths in shipped code
